ga_2(){return"The account is optional. Without an account, Mirinu asks for neither your name nor your email address. Your library, your ratings and your settings stay on your device: in the app on Android, in the browser's storage on app.mirinu.ch, without cookies. A file you import is read on the spot and sent nowhere."},
ga_1(){return"Before a code is emailed, a Cloudflare anti-bot check (Turnstile) reads your IP address and information about your browser. The relay also asks Cloudflare whether the domain of your address (what follows the @) receives email; neither your full address nor your IP address goes there. To curb abuse, the relay also counts requests per email address and per IP address, in an unreadable form erased the next day. These protections rest on the legitimate interest in protecting the service."},
gZU(){return"Your data is on your devices and, if you use sync or an account, on the Mirinu relay: an encrypted copy of your library and, with an account, your email address, encrypted."},
ga_5(){return"Updated on November 10, 2026."},
ga_b(){return"Updated on November 10, 2026."},
gZX(){return"Updated on November 10, 2026."},
ga_4(){return"The relay runs on a server rented from Infomaniak (Switzerland), which also hosts the contact@mirinu.ch mailbox. The same server serves mirinu.ch and app.mirinu.ch, without keeping a log of visits. Cloudflare (United States) is used only for the Turnstile bot check and to check the domain of an email address. For signing in with Google, Google (United States) is involved too. Cloudflare and Google take part in the Data Privacy Framework, which Switzerland and the EU recognize for data sent to the United States."},
ga_3(){return"Mirinu does not keep your IP address: to curb abuse, the relay counts requests per address, in an unreadable form erased the next day. It erases a sync without an account 180 days after its last sync, and a space left empty after one day. The relay's nightly backups keep what is erased for up to 7 more days. An email you send is kept while your request is handled."},
